WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.793
The equipment design envelope, intended
operating range

2
00:00:03.913 --> 00:00:07.844
and demonstrated test coverage are related
but different.

3
00:00:07.964 --> 00:00:13.206
A manufacturer rating does not prove every
use inside it has been qualified.

4
00:00:13.326 --> 00:00:16.705
Conversely, deliberately exceeding that
rating is

5
00:00:16.825 --> 00:00:19.859
not a sensible interpretation of worst
case.

6
00:00:19.979 --> 00:00:22.945
Keep the proposed range justified and
safe.

7
00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:26.255
For a vessel, consider how fill volume,

8
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:29.063
agitation and heating demand interact.

9
00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:32.769
A small fill might challenge immersion or
overshoot,

10
00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:36.199
while a larger load challenges heating
response.

11
00:00:36.319 --> 00:00:40.388
These are hypotheses to evaluate against
the actual design.

12
00:00:40.508 --> 00:00:44.220
Document why a chosen combination is
representative

13
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.754
and what remains outside the study.

14
00:00:47.374 --> 00:00:51.305
A matrix makes selected conditions and
omissions visible.

15
00:00:51.425 --> 00:00:55.457
Three speeds and two justified loads give
six combinations

16
00:00:55.577 --> 00:00:58.819
if all pairs are required by the teaching
plan.

17
00:00:58.939 --> 00:01:03.352
This arithmetic does not prescribe six
tests for real equipment.

18
00:01:03.472 --> 00:01:08.656
Sampling, repetitions and any reduced
design need their own reasoned basis.

19
00:01:09.276 --> 00:01:12.656
A planned disturbance can examine
robustness only

20
00:01:12.776 --> 00:01:16.569
when the challenge and expected recovery
are justified.

21
00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:19.447
Never turn off a plant utility or defeat

22
00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:22.878
a protection device based on a training
example.

23
00:01:22.998 --> 00:01:27.243
Engineering defines a safe simulation or
controlled method,

24
00:01:27.363 --> 00:01:31.708
and the record states what that method
represents and excludes.
